  "Question": "Peter’s family ordered a \\(12\\)-slice pizza for dinner. Peter ate one slice and shared another slice equally with his brother Paul. What fraction of the pizza did Peter eat?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{24} \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{12} \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{8} \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{6} \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{4} \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "One slice is \\(1/12\\) of the pizza. Peter also ate half of another slice, which is\n\\[\n\\frac1{12}\\div2=\\frac1{24}\n\\]\nof the pizza. His total share was\n\\[\n\\frac1{12}+\\frac1{24}\n=\\frac2{24}+\\frac1{24}\n=\\frac3{24}=\\boxed{\\frac18},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
